Step-by-Step Solution
Step 1: Understanding the Clues

The challenge provides two important hints:

    "Where are cookies stored?"

    "Do you know how to use the web inspector?"

Plus the developer's statement: "once you login, you never have to log-out again"

This immediately tells us we're dealing with persistent session cookies that can be viewed in the browser's developer tools.
Step 2: Initial Reconnaissance

When visiting the site, we see a login page for "The New Twitter" (a social media platform):

    URL: http://dolphin-cove.picoctf.net:[port]/login

    Login form with username/password fields

    Link to register page at /register

Step 3: Attempting Registration

    Click the Register link to access /register

    Create a test account (e.g., username: test, password: test)

    After submitting, the site redirects back to the login page

    Registration appears successful

Step 4: Testing Login with Test Account

    Try logging in with the newly created test credentials

    Check cookies using browser developer tools:

        Open Developer Tools (F12)

        Go to Storage tab (Firefox) or Application tab (Chrome)

        Check Cookies section

        Run in console: console.log(document.cookie)

Result: Cookies remain empty - test account doesn't generate a session cookie
Step 5: Trying Common Development Credentials

Since this is an application "still under development," try common default credentials:

    admin:admin

    admin:password

    admin:password123

    test:test

    user:user

Success! Using credentials:

    Username: admin

    Password: password

The login is successful and redirects to the main page.
Step 6: Locating the Flag

After successful admin login, check for the flag:

Option A - Check Cookies:
javascript

console.log(document.cookie);

or navigate to Storage → Cookies → select the site URL

Option B - Check Page Source:
